\section*{Epistemic Closure Theorem for the CMD--Astrophysical Coupling Architecture}

\subsection*{Preliminaries}

Let $(\mathcal{H}, \langle \cdot , \cdot \rangle)$ be a Hilbert space representing the full
state of the coupled CMD--MHD engine, including SPH particle fields, MHD tensor
bundles, and mucosal immune state-machine configurations.  
Let
\[
X(t) \in \mathcal{H}
\]
denote the evolving system state under the dynamical law
\[
\frac{dX}{dt} = \mathcal{A}X + \mathcal{N}(X),
\]
where $\mathcal{A}$ is a linear cross-scale operator and $\mathcal{N}$ is a nonlinear
response operator incorporating RIE, NHD, and immune-transition dynamics.

Define the stress-test convergence functionals:
\[
\Phi_{P}(t),\qquad \Phi_{C}(t),\qquad \Phi_{E}(t),
\]
corresponding respectively to Parsob convergence, Cerob convergence, and Error
cohergence.

Let $\Lambda$ denote the Ephemeral Evidence Ledger mapping each execution epoch
$k$ to a cryptographic hash of its telemetry:
\[
\Lambda(k) = \mathrm{Hash}\!\left(X_k(t), \Phi_{P,k}, \Phi_{C,k}, \Phi_{E,k}\right).
\]

\subsection*{Lemma 1 (Boundedness)}
Assume:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item $\mathcal{A}$ generates a strongly continuous semigroup satisfying
    \[
    \|\mathrm{e}^{t\mathcal{A}}\| \le C e^{\omega t}, \qquad C>0,\;\omega\ge 0,
    \]
    \item $\mathcal{N}$ is locally Lipschitz and dissipative:
    \[
    \langle \mathcal{N}(X), X \rangle \le -\alpha \|X\|^2 + \beta,
    \qquad \alpha>0,\;\beta\ge 0.
    \]
\end{enumerate}
Then there exists $M>0$ such that
\[
\sup_{t\ge 0} \|X(t)\| \le M.
\]

\subsection*{Lemma 2 (Convergence of Stress Functionals)}
Under the hypotheses of Lemma~1 and Continuous Yield Mode operation:
\[
\Phi_{P}(t) \to 0,\qquad
\Phi_{C}(t) \text{ is bounded},\qquad
\sup_{t\ge 0}\Phi_{E}(t) < \infty.
\]

\subsection*{Lemma 3 (Ledger Integrity)}
If $\Lambda$ is implemented using collision-resistant cryptographic hashing and
append-only storage, then each ledger entry $\Lambda(k)$ is an immutable witness
of the corresponding bounded and convergent execution epoch.

\subsection*{Theorem (Epistemic Closure)}
Assume Lemmas~1--3. Then the CMD--Astrophysical Coupling Architecture is
\emph{epistemically closed} in the following sense:

\begin{enumerate}
    \item \textbf{Mathematical Closure.}
    All trajectories $X(t)$ remain in a bounded subset of $\mathcal{H}$, and their
    qualitative behavior is fully determined by $\mathcal{A}$ and $\mathcal{N}$.

    \item \textbf{Empirical Closure.}
    Every high-load execution satisfies the convergence properties encoded in
    $\Phi_{P}$, $\Phi_{C}$, and $\Phi_{E}$, with no untracked drift or unbounded
    error.

    \item \textbf{Evidential Closure.}
    Every validated run is permanently recorded in $\Lambda$, producing a
    tamper-evident chain of custody for all telemetry and validation data.
\end{enumerate}

Therefore, for any scientific claim derived from the CMD engine’s operation,
there exists a corresponding triple:
\[
\left(
\text{boundedness proof},\;
\text{convergence telemetry},\;
\text{ledger hash}
\right),
\]
ensuring that the claim cannot be asserted without a matching mathematical,
empirical, and cryptographic witness. This constitutes epistemic closure of the
architecture.